I attended the 2026 S.-T. Yau High School Science Award in Mathematics.

My research explores how to manage tourism in Yinshanmen, a historic neighborhood in Zhenjiang, China. I developed a dynamic network flow model that considers both tourist movement and residents' tolerance. Using Python simulations, I tested different visitor management strategies to find a balance between tourism and residents' daily lives.

This folder contains my research paper and supporting code.
